{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.72,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["J2", "U2"],
      "pins": ["J2.A4", "U2.1", "U2.2"],
      "nets": ["VBUS", "+5V"],
      "observed": "On the MCU sheet the USB-C receptacle J2 VBUS pin (A4) is wired to a node that carries BOTH the global label 'VBUS' and the global label '+5V' (joined by a junction dot). On the Power sheet the TPS2121RUXR U2 has IN2 (pin 2) = '+5V' and OUT (pin 1) = 'VBUS'. Because the two names are shorted together at J2, the mux input (+5V) and the mux output (VBUS, which feeds the buck) become the same net.",
      "expected": "Per the spec the power mux must arbitrate the two supplies: USB VBUS should be the '+5V' net feeding IN2 only, and the mux OUT should be a separate 'VBUS' net feeding the buck. The two nets must not be joined upstream of the mux.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "mcu.kicad_sch (page 3/4): J2 pin A4 wire shows global labels '+5V' (green arrow) and 'VBUS' (label box) tied together at a junction"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "power.kicad_sch (page 7): U2 TPS2121RUXR pin 2 IN2 = '+5V', pin 1 OUT = 'VBUS'"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "IN1 (pin 7) wired to the barrel-jack +12V net, IN2 (pin 2) wired to USB +5V/VBUS, with a common OUT feeding the board's unregulated VBUS rail that supplies the buck converter"}
      ],
      "impact": "The TPS2121RUXR power mux is defeated: its IN2 and OUT are shorted through the USB connector. The buck input 'VBUS' is hard-tied to USB 5V, so seamless switchover cannot occur, and when the 12 V barrel jack is connected the mux tries to push 12 V onto the USB VBUS pin (back-feed into the host / supply conflict), violating the intended arbitration architecture.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic otherwise matches the spec (correct parts, SPI/CS mapping, heater high-side switch with FAULT only to a test point, buck FB tied to +3V3, 5.1k CC pulldowns, 51.1k ILIM, 3.9uH inductor), but the USB VBUS pin is given both the '+5V' and 'VBUS' global labels, shorting the power-mux input to its output and bypassing the TPS2121RUXR arbitration the design relies on."
}

